  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nAmplified mid level flow with an anomalously strong ridge over the \neastern CONUS will be temporarily flattened as a shortwave passes \nthru the northern Great Lakes today into southeast Canada tonight. \nThe ridge will re-establish over the area Friday into the first part \nof the weekend. \n\nThis will provide continued conditions and seasonably warm daytime \nhighs for our area. With good radiational cooling, areas of river \nvalley fog will develop this morning. Have also undercut afternoon \ndewpoints from guidance.\n\nThe ridge will slide to the east with mid level flow backing and\nmoisture increases ahead of a surface cold front that will move \nthrough Sunday night. This will bring the next chance for \nprecipitation, along with cooler temperatures for early next week.",
